  "title": "S4: skill scorecard with marginal value and redundancy: skill \u00d7 role \u00d7 task class \u00d7 complexity \u00d7 model \u00d7 workflow strategy, role-without-skill vs role-with-skill comparison, redundancy between co-used skills; reporting only (v3)",
  "spec": "Program brief .orchestrator/roadmap-skills.md P14, P15, P16, P24, P25, P30 (P37 stage 4). Depends on T-0894 (run context carries skills_exposed / skills_used / skill tokens; skill_scorecard.py exists with use_rate and overhead) and T-0913 (skills_selected, skill_recovery_rate). Facts: run rows (bus.log_run) carry role, task, tier/executor (model via attribution.model_of), usage tokens, usd, duration_s; lineage roots via attribution.lineage; task_class via attribution.task_class; complexity band via attribution.band; workflow strategy via strategy.derive(task, tasks); gate/review outcomes live on task pipelines (gate_reds, review verdicts on review tasks with inputs[0]); read_economy gate rows carry per-call paths and tools; promotion CRITERIA min_samples 20.\nDo:\n1. skill_scorecard.py: `usage_rows(root)` = one row per run with skills_used, plus the lineage's outcome (first_pass, fix_rounds, gate_reds, review_request_changes, accepted, accepted_tokens, accepted_usd, latency_s, tool_calls when known) and the dimensions (role, task_class, band, model, strategy, repo = \"orchestrator\"). `by_skill(root, group_by=(\"role\",\"task_class\"))` aggregates per skill \u00d7 the chosen dimensions with n and every metric; unknown values are None, never 0.\n2. Marginal value (P15): `marginal(root, skill, group_by=(\"role\",\"task_class\"), min_samples=cfg)`: for each group, compare runs of the same role/class WITH the skill used vs WITHOUT (neither used nor selected): deltas for first_pass, fix_rounds, accepted_tokens, accepted_usd, latency_s, plus the skill's own token overhead (l2 tokens per use); returns {\"insufficient\": True, \"n_with\", \"n_without\"} below min_samples on either side; otherwise deltas with both n. A `verdict` field: \"valuable\" (quality delta \u2265 0 and cost delta \u2264 0, or quality delta > +0.05 with cost delta within +10%), \"neutral\", \"costly\" (tokens up without quality change), \"harmful\" (quality down) \u2014 reporting only, no state changes (Stage 10 acts on it).\n3. Redundancy (P16): `redundancy(root)`: for skill pairs co-used in one run: count of co-uses, overlap proxy = fraction of paths read by both (from read_economy gate rows joined by session/task when available, else None), duplicated script invocations (same script:<path> tool in both skills' declared tools), unique-findings proxy = None with a note (needs Stage 6 evidence sharing). Reported as a table with n.\n4. Model and workflow interaction (P24/P25): by_skill with group_by (\"model\",) and (\"strategy\",\"task_class\") available through the CLI: `orchestrator scorecard --skills [--by role,task_class|model|strategy,task_class] [--marginal <skill>] [--redundancy]`; `--economy` skills block gains the top-3 \"costly\"/\"harmful\" verdicts when any group has sufficient samples.\n5. docs/skill-intelligence/05-scorecard.md (\u226470 lines): formulas, dimensions, the verdict rules, what is a proxy, min_samples, revert path (reporting only).\nTests (unittest): tests/test_skill_scorecard.py::test_usage_rows_join_lineage_outcomes_and_dimensions, ::test_by_skill_groups_and_none_for_unknown, ::test_marginal_insufficient_below_min_samples, ::test_marginal_verdicts_valuable_costly_harmful, ::test_redundancy_pairs_and_script_overlap, ::test_cli_by_model_and_strategy. Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally. Do not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.\n\nSPEC v2 (2026-09-23 06:05) after spec review T-0931 (request_changes), binding on top of v1:\n- orchestrator/skill_scorecard.py and tests/test_skill_scorecard.py already exist (from T-0894 and T-0913) and are EXTENDED, never replaced: add usage_rows/by_skill/marginal/redundancy next to the existing build()/format_report(); the three existing tests (test_use_rate_and_overhead_ratio_per_skill, test_skill_tokens_per_accepted_task, test_skill_recovery_rate_and_reduction) must keep passing and are listed in acceptance.\n- CLI grouping: a new flag `--group-by <dims>` (comma-separated, validated against the allowed dimension names role, task_class, band, model, strategy, repo) applies to --skills mode only; the existing single-choice `--by` is untouched. `--marginal <skill>` and `--redundancy` remain as specified.\n- redundancy()'s overlap proxy reads .orchestrator/runs/jev/gate.jsonl rows directly (fields session, task, tool, tool_target) and joins them to runs by task id; read_economy.summary() is not used for this.\n- Acceptance adds: the three existing tests stay green; tests/test_skill_scorecard.py::test_cli_by_model_and_strategy uses --group-by.\n\nSPEC v3 (2026-09-23 06:45) after spec review T-0934 (round 2; three points folded in, further review waived by the Planner, verdict set to approve):\n- redundancy() overlap proxy, precise: for each skill build its aggregate path-set from gate rows of runs where that skill was the ONLY skill used (single-skill runs); the overlap of a pair = |A \u2229 B| / |A \u222a B| over those aggregate sets; co-use count is reported separately from runs where both were used; when either skill has no single-skill runs the overlap is None with note \"no single-skill runs\".\n- usage_rows() resolves each run's owning execute-root lineage with the same task-graph membership logic as strategy._root_id (walk fix_round_for and inputs/parent links to the execute root of the task graph), so scout, spec_review and review runs inherit the outcome of the execute root they served; runs with no execute root keep outcome None.\n- CLI: --group-by, --marginal and --redundancy passed without --skills are rejected with ap.error in the existing mode-conflict style; an unknown --group-by dimension is rejected the same way. Test tests/test_skill_scorecard.py::test_cli_rejects_skill_flags_without_skills_mode.",
